implementationPlan.description:
DoD 1 — extend packages/mcp/src/index.ts with the HTTP surface. This is the entire production change.

Add, in the style the file already uses (explicit named blocks per area, never `export *`):
  export { createHttpMcpAdapter } from "./http/http-server.js";
  export type { HttpAdapterOptions, HttpMcpAdapter, HttpAuthOutcome, HttpDispatchPort } from "./http/http-server.js";
  export type { HttpSessionPort } from "./http/http-session.js";

Every specifier is NodeNext ".js" resolving into src/http/** — that is DoD 1's explicit requirement and it is what makes the published root load under plain Node rather than only under vitest.

Place the HTTP block after the stdio blocks and keep the existing stdio exports byte-identical. DoD 5 requires the pre-existing stdio surface to survive unchanged; a re-export that shadows or drops one of them must fail, and the cheapest way to not shadow anything is to not touch those lines.

NOTHING ELSE CHANGES. DoD 6: no file under packages/mcp/src/http/ and no file under apps/ may be modified. If a name does not re-export cleanly, that is a finding to report — not a licence to edit http-server.ts.

implementationPlan.note:
DoD 1 landed. Appended exactly two source specifiers, both NodeNext ".js" into src/http/**:
  export { createHttpMcpAdapter } from "./http/http-server.js";
  export type { HttpAdapterOptions, HttpAuthOutcome, HttpDispatchPort, HttpMcpAdapter } from "./http/http-server.js";
  export type { HttpSessionPort } from "./http/http-session.js";

`git diff -- packages/mcp/src/index.ts` is purely additive (@@ -25,3 +25,11 @@, eight + lines, zero - lines), so every pre-existing stdio line is byte-identical per DoD 5. index.js untouched — it is `export * from "./index.ts";` and needs nothing.

Measured after the edit:
- pnpm --filter @moe/mcp typecheck exit 0.
- Runtime namespace from packages/mcp cwd under plain Node --experimental-strip-types: COUNT 13 -> 14, typeof createHttpMcpAdapter === "function". The one added key is createHttpMcpAdapter and nothing else, which is the positive proof that the explicit named block did NOT leak the three other runtime values living in http-server.ts (HTTP_LISTED_TOOLS, LOOPBACK_HOSTNAMES, MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION_HEADER). Those three become the negative control in the step-3 test.

Nothing under packages/mcp/src/http/ or apps/ touched.
